            "paragraph": "The AIM-Hub model, formerly known as AIM/CGE35 (Asia-Pacific Integrated Model/Computable General Equilibrium), is a one-year-step recursive-dynamic general equilibrium model that has global coverage, including 17 regions and 42 industrial classifications, with detailed agricultural sectors to assess bioenergy and land-use competition accurately. The model maximizes production sector profits using multi-nested constant-elasticity-of-substitution functions for input prices and models household expenditures with a linear expenditure system function, updated recursively by income elasticity. It includes GHGs such as CO2 from energy and non-energy sources, CH4, N2O and fluorinated gases.",
